-- title:
--   Row projections only see the odd part
-- statement:
--   Sign matrices are Boolean $m\times m$ matrices; $\mathrm{row}(\sigma)$ is the matrix with entries $\sigma_i$ in row $i$, $S_i$ denotes row $i$ of $S$, and $\oplus$ is entrywise XOR. For a function $F$ on sign matrices and a row $i$, let
--   $$
--   (\mathcal R_iF)(S)=\mathbb E_\sigma\,s(\sigma_i)\,F\bigl(\mathrm{row}(\sigma)\oplus S\bigr),
--   $$
--   with $s(0)=1$, $s(1)=-1$. Then $\mathcal R_i(F_{\mathrm{odd}})=\mathcal R_iF$, where $F_{\mathrm{odd}}(S)=\frac12(F(S)-F(\bar S))$.
--
--   The even part of $F$ is invisible to row projections.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/PatternProjections.lean#L13-L27

